title: Overview - Vocabularies & Markers (v1.0)

The v1.0 conceptual model in one picture: a ''marker'' is a tiddler, a ''vocabulary'' is a tag set, and a tiddler ''activates'' a vocabulary via its type field or a pragma.

[img[cm-v1-concept.svg]]

!! The three pieces

; ① A marker is a tiddler
: Tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker` plus the vocab tiddler's title (e.g. `[[vocab/fountain]]`). The `kind` field picks one of five matching modes; `open` is the literal that triggers the match. Output is controlled by `element`, `classes`, `attributes`. Body parsing is controlled by `mode`, `paragraph-marker`, `end-string`, `emit-open`, `body-raw`.

; ② Vocabularies group markers
: One meta tiddler per vocab, tagged `$:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary`. ''Title convention:'' `vocab/<lowercase-caption>` — the registry's `activate()` resolves a name by direct lookup, no filter walk (about 33× faster than the pre-beta-29 path). Optional fields: `disable-core-rules` (whitespace-separated TW core wikirule names to remove), `front-matter: yes` (consume YAML at parser pos 0).

; ③ Two activation paths
:* ''Type field:'' `type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Markdown`. Persisted, single `.tid` on disk (thanks to `startup/fix-vocab-type.js`).
:* ''Pragma:'' `\importcustom [tag[vocab/fountain]]` at the top of a tiddler. The filter runs over `[all[shadows+tiddlers]]` automatically.
: A bare `text/vnd.tiddlywiki` (no `;vocab=`) implicitly activates `vocab/default`. Listing any `;vocab=` makes Default no longer implicit — add it explicitly if you want its markers.

!! The five marker kinds

; glyph
: Single fire at line start; whole line is body. Example: [[vocab/default/DOT]] (`. text` → `<div class="wltc wltc-dot">text</div>`).
; glyph-level
: N repetitions of `open` → emits class `wltc-lN` (default `max-level: 4`). Example: [[vocab/default/ANGLE]] (`»`, `»»`, ...).
; word
: Keyword block; single line (`mode: inline`) or multi-block. Example: [[vocab/fountain/INT]] (`INT. KITCHEN — MORNING`).
; inline-pair
: `open` ... `close` anywhere on a line. Example: [[vocab/default/SLASH]] (`/° ... °/`).
; list-item
: Consecutive items collapse into one container (`ul` / `ol` / `dl` / `blockquote`); nesting via indent. Example: [[vocab/markdown/ITEM-DASH]] (`- ...`).

!! Composition rules

* Same `open` in two active vocabs → ''LAST listed wins''. `;vocab=A,B` lets B's marker take over a shared `open`.
* `disable-core-rules` removes the listed TW core wikirules ''for that tiddler only'' (via `parser.amendRules`). Lets Markdown claim `_`, `~~`, `|`; lets Fountain claim `!` and `#`.
* Inactive marker matches fall through to plain text. They do NOT shadow competing core rules in unrelated tiddlers (`findNextMatch` filter, gated on `_cmPragmasDone`).
* Secure-by-default: `iframe` gets `sandbox=""`, `object`/`embed`/`frame`/`frameset` are denied, `javascript:` URLs are stripped. Opt out with `allow-unsafe: yes`. See [[Custom Markup Security]].

